Input: {"question": "What is the language of the film \"Devatha\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 0, "end": 68, "text": "Devata (1941 film) Devata is a 1941 Telugu drama film directed by B."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 69, "end": 71, "text": "N."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 72, "end": 78, "text": "Reddi."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 79, "end": 175, "text": "The huge success of this film lead to the making of more films with the same title in 1964 by B."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 176, "end": 205, "text": "Padmanabham and in 1982 by D."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 206, "end": 216, "text": "Ramanaidu."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 217, "end": 269, "text": "The film was remade in Malayalam as \"Pavappettaval\"."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 270, "end": 356, "text": "Venugopala Murthy returns to his native village from England after passing law school."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 357, "end": 410, "text": "His mother Mangamma and sister Seetha are very happy."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 411, "end": 503, "text": "Venu is attracted towards Lakshmi, daughter of Venkaiah, who works as servant in the family."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d00", "start": 504, "end": 573, "text": "He takes advantage of the sleeping Lakshmi and promises to marry her."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d01", "start": 0, "end": 26, "text": "Babu Srinivas Edited by K."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d01", "start": 27, "end": 218, "text": "Eshwar Music by Dhina Production company Sri Lakshmi Mookambika Films Release date 30 November 2001 (2001-11-30) Running time 145 minutes Country India Language Marathi Grama Devathe (transl."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d01", "start": 219, "end": 326, "text": "Village Deity) is a 2001 Indian Marathi-language Hindu devotional film written and directed by Sai Prakash."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d01", "start": 327, "end": 370, "text": "It stars Meena, Prema, Sai Kumar, and Roja."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d01", "start": 371, "end": 480, "text": "The film was dubbed in Tamil as Angala Parameswari, in Telugu as Grama Devatha, and in Hindi as Maa Devi Maa."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d01", "start": 481, "end": 529, "text": "Plot [edit] On the request of the Hindu deity..."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d02", "start": 0, "end": 67, "text": "Devata (1941 film) Devata is a 1941 Hindi drama film directed by B."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d02", "start": 68, "end": 70, "text": "N."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d02", "start": 71, "end": 77, "text": "Reddi."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d02", "start": 78, "end": 174, "text": "The huge success of this film lead to the making of more films with the same title in 1964 by B."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d02", "start": 175, "end": 204, "text": "Padmanabham and in 1982 by D."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0130-0c24f4852e8a:d02", "start": 205, "end": 215, "text": "Ramanaidu."}, "D3S7": {"document_num